        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0602" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg518"/>

                <head>No. 267.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Presson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Collector’s Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Gloucester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-08-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 9, 1886</date>. [Received
                        August 11.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am requested to forward the inclosed
                    affidavit of Capt. Daniel McDonald of schooner Hereward, of Gloucester, in
                    regard to his detention at Cape Canso, Nova Scotia, July 2.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. S. PRESSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Collector.</hi></signed></closer>




